From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:47:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/companion: pack and show the ACNH companion in a split's
 band

A profile with companion.json opts its game into Eden Duo's companion: the
build derives the interface manifest from the vendored MSBT strings, bundles
the profile's build-ID and input-gate rows with the component licenses, and
defines DM_COMPANION for the Swift part. The renderer compiles into every app;
without the condition its bridge answers NULL and the front end keeps its
empty band, so an app for any other game shows nothing. gen_build.py passes
the module's C++ and ObjC++ sources through.

The iOS root puts the companion's hosting controller in the band a split gives
it, with the pad floating over it, and the pad hands the band's non-key taps
through (DmGamepad.m hitTest). front_run tells the guest-memory reader that
the modules are loaded before the guest starts.

The harness stands in an empty view for the Swift companion and checks that a
tap on a clear part of the band reaches it.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The ACNH companion: Eden Duo's reader and the band a phone standing up shows it in; nxnative carries it on feat/acnh-companion
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

